diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/README.md b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..495cd54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+# Character resource transaction journal (development)
+
+This product component owns the persistent resource transaction state shared by
+the normal application and retained Recovery. It does not download packages,
+write NOR, choose a boot partition, or verify package authenticity. A single
+coordinator owns each handle and serializes every load/save and its associated
+filesystem work. The mounted NAND service remains an app-lifetime singleton.
+
+## Durable record
+
+The trusted coordinator uses `/nand/muse-character/transaction.0` and
+`transaction.1`, with `transaction.partial` as uncommitted scratch. These paths
+never come from downloaded manifests. Do not reuse the protected initial image
+as the per-update backup; both are separate from the journal.
+
+Each committed slot is exactly 512 bytes, little endian:
+
+| Offset | Size | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | 8 | ASCII `MCHARJ01` |
+| 8 | 4 | Record version, 1 |
+| 12 | 4 | Phase enum |
+| 16 | 8 | Monotonic sequence, starting at 1 |
+| 24 | 4 | Live `ui_apps` partition address |
+| 28 | 4 | Complete partition capacity |
+| 32 | 4 | New image size |
+| 36 | 4 | Reserved zero |
+| 40 | 64 | Job identifier, NUL terminated and zero padded |
+| 104 | 32 | New image SHA-256 |
+| 136 | 32 | Complete old partition backup SHA-256 |
+| 168 | 96 | Compatibility identifier, NUL terminated and zero padded |
+| 264 | 64 | Character version, NUL terminated and zero padded |
+| 328 | 180 | Reserved zero |
+| 508 | 4 | IEEE CRC-32 of bytes 0..507 |
+
+CRC detects damaged records; it is **not** a signature or authentication.
+Job/version strings accept ASCII letters, digits, dot, underscore and hyphen.
+SHA-256 verification of actual files and package compatibility remains the
+coordinator's responsibility before creating a record or performing a write.
+
+Save order is temp write, `fflush`, `fsync`, close, exact read-back comparison,
+NAND sync, rename over the inactive committed slot, NAND sync. If save returns
+an error, reload before deciding what happened. A failed final sync may leave
+the new slot visible; it never authorizes a subsequent NOR write by itself.
+
+Both committed slots must be valid and consecutive once there is history. One
+slot alone is allowed only for the first STAGED sequence 1. A corrupt slot,
+missing later history, duplicate sequence or illegal phase transition holds
+Recovery; never silently prefer a possibly older safe-looking record. Partial
+files are ignored. Neither create nor load formats NAND or deletes history.
+
+## State and side-effect ordering
+
+1. `STAGED`: verified new image persisted. Candidate-only compatibility cannot
+   authorize installation, even if its string exactly matches firmware.
+2. `BACKUP_READY`: complete old partition backed up, synced and verified.
+3. `WRITING`: save succeeds **before the first NOR erase/write**.
+4. `TRIAL`: new NOR read-back verified; save succeeds before selecting the app.
+5. `CONFIRMED`: app has validated the expected interface and first frame. A
+   successful download or boot alone must not cause this transition.
+
+Recovery encountering WRITING, TRIAL or RESTORING must verify the old backup,
+persist RESTORING if needed, restore and read-back verify the complete old
+partition, and only then persist ROLLED_BACK and boot the app. Interruption
+during restore repeats restoration. STAGED and BACKUP_READY can be canceled
+before any NOR write. A subsequent job starts only after a terminal phase and
+continues the sequence; a reused job ID is rejected.
+
+The boot decision function deliberately permits restoration independent of the
+new compatibility identifier, but requires an identical live partition address
+and capacity. Corrupt metadata or a changed layout requires USB maintenance.
+
+## Integration status
+
+The journal C code and filesystem implementation are included in application
+and Recovery builds. Recovery has a pre-Bridge automatic-boot guard, disabled
+by default under `CONFIG_IRIS_FACTORY_CHARACTER_BOOT_GUARD`. When enabled it
+holds automatic boot on mount failure or pending/corrupt transactions and keeps
+USB services reachable. This development guard is **not** a complete updater:
+physical acceptance and corrupt-journal repair policy must be completed before
+enabling it in a release. No current candidate
+package is staged into this journal or installed.
+
+The Recovery transaction engine now sequences verified backup, WRITING record,
+write/read-back, TRIAL record, and rollback. Its synchronous callbacks hold the
+shared writer across backup, failed writes and recovery. The product adapter
+uses fixed `candidate-ui.bin`, `previous-ui.bin` and `previous-ui.partial` paths;
+it never overwrites `factory-ui.bin`. Recovery's dedicated CHARACTER owner
+creates a single data plan for the live `ui_apps` partition, using the existing
+erase/write/read-back implementation and no partition-table component.
+
+With the development boot guard enabled, WRITING/TRIAL/RESTORING records are
+restored automatically before Bridge resume. STAGED/BACKUP_READY remain held
+because candidate admission is closed. The application boot owner now verifies
+the active image, arms Recovery before rendering, and confirms only after native
+first-frame/binding/flush/error checks. New installation, corrupt-journal repair,
+voice scheduling and physical power-loss acceptance remain outstanding.
+Do not release this as a complete updater.
+
+ROLLED_BACK is a durable return intent, not a terminal record. Recovery verifies
+the complete old NOR image and ota_0 executable, selects ota_0 **before** saving
+ROLLBACK_TRIAL, then releases the writer and restarts. A power cut between boot
+selection and journal save boots the app with ROLLED_BACK; the app completes that
+same trial transition. ROLLBACK_TRIAL arms Recovery before rendering; a failed
+restored-app boot stays in Recovery instead of repeatedly booting a bad UI.
+Successful old-UI validation saves terminal ROLLBACK_CONFIRMED. A new job cannot
+start before the restored application confirms. Appended phase values 9 and 10
+retain the existing 512-byte encoding, but old prototype binaries reject them;
+install matching app and Recovery together through system-update.
+
+USB maintenance service 0x1202 method 6 accepts CANCEL_UNWRITTEN_CHARACTER_V1
+only before NOR writes. Method 7 accepts RETRY_CHARACTER_RECOVERY_V1, starts a
+serialized worker and returns promptly; method 8 (empty payload) returns cached
+state/error (0 idle, 1 running, 2 failed). Retry restores WRITING/TRIAL/RESTORING
+from the verified backup, or retries ROLLBACK_TRIAL only after a full old-NOR hash
+check and a durable transition back to ROLLED_BACK. No candidate install is
+admitted. Corrupt journals remain held; retry cannot format, discard records or
+unconditionally release the writer. HTTP/Bridge/Anna cannot authorize these
+USB-only methods.
+
+Explicit USB method 7 also accepts `REPAIR_CHARACTER_JOURNAL_V1` for an
+unreadable history. This is separate from ordinary retry: it requires a mounted
+NAND and the existing protected `factory-ui.record` plus complete `factory-ui.bin`
+to match the live partition and full hash. No backup is created or formatted.
+Recovery reserves local source tags `muse-journal-repair-v1` /
+`protected-initial-repair`; remote cpack compatibility cannot select this source.
+
+The store preserves `transaction.0` / `.1` and any earlier repair history.
+For a unique job it archives the previous selector byte-for-byte (even when
+damaged) as `repair-<job>.prior`, publishes an immutable 512-byte
+`repair-<job>.seed`, then atomically publishes the same record as
+`repair-selector.record`. Every publication includes fsync, readback and NAND
+sync around rename. A seed is sequence 1, RESTORING, with full partition size
+and matching image/backup hashes. The selector must match the immutable seed.
+Before publication unreadable history remains held; after publication missing
+transition slots mean RESTORING intent, never an empty journal. Transitions use
+`repair-<job>.0` / `.1` and retain the ordinary consecutive-record checks.
+Selected seed/selector/slot corruption stays held and needs another unique
+explicit repair; healthy or absent histories cannot be replaced by this API.
+Repair restores protected initial resources through the existing Recovery
+writer and rollback trial/first-frame confirmation. It cannot reconstruct the
+last pre-failure role from damaged metadata. It never claims that role survived.
+Matching app and Recovery must be installed together; all consumers must honor
+the selector. Host sync-fault tests do not establish physical power-loss safety.
+
+Host tests execute the actual C encoding, state decisions and filesystem code,
+injecting sync failures before/after rename. They cover damaged/truncated slots,
+512 individual bit flips, candidate rejection, backup prerequisites, rollback
+states and repeated transactions. Host filesystem faults do not establish
+LittleFS atomicity, NAND durability or physical power-loss acceptance.
+
+Protected initial-resource restore uses the same transaction phases and wire
+encoding. The product reserves `compat_version=muse-protected-initial-v1` AND
+`character_version=protected-initial` as a LOCAL source tag. The helper
+`mosaico_character_record_is_initial()` requires a valid record and both tags;
+this classification is not authorization. External cpack validation rejects this
+compatibility value. Firmware's trusted installation gate remains mandatory and
+currently closed for both sources.
+
+The app prepares a verified unpadded image from its existing protected complete
+partition backup at `factory-ui-restore.bin`. Recovery selects that fixed source
+for locally tagged records; downloaded jobs use `candidate-ui.bin`. Neither
+source can supply a filename or redirect the writer. Recovery hashes the exact
+source before erase and writes only through the existing character writer.
+It first backs up CURRENT ui_apps into `previous-ui.bin`; an unconfirmed or
+failed initial restore rolls back to that current role, not to the factory
+backup. The protected factory backup is never used as mutable rollback scratch.
+Application first-frame confirmation remains required for an initial restore.
+Install matching app and Recovery before enabling this source. No user-facing
+restore request or physical acceptance is provided by this component alone.
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal.c b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7fa4a3b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal.c
@@ -0,0 +1,166 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#include "mosaico_character_journal.h"
+#include <string.h>
+
+enum { CRC_OFFSET = 508, SECTOR_BYTES = 4096, MIN_IMAGE_BYTES = 96 };
+static const uint8_t magic[8] = {'M','C','H','A','R','J','0','1'};
+
+static uint32_t crc32(const uint8_t *data, size_t bytes)
+{
+    uint32_t crc = UINT32_MAX;
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < bytes; ++i) {
+        crc ^= data[i];
+        for (unsigned b = 0; b < 8; ++b)
+            crc = (crc >> 1) ^ (0xedb88320U & (0U - (crc & 1U)));
+    }
+    return ~crc;
+}
+static void put32(uint8_t *p, uint32_t value)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) p[i] = (uint8_t)(value >> (8 * i));
+}
+static uint32_t get32(const uint8_t *p)
+{
+    return (uint32_t)p[0] | (uint32_t)p[1] << 8 | (uint32_t)p[2] << 16 | (uint32_t)p[3] << 24;
+}
+static bool identifier(const char *s, size_t capacity)
+{
+    const char *end = memchr(s, 0, capacity);
+    if (!end || end == s) return false;
+    for (const char *p = s; p < end; ++p)
+        if (!((*p >= 'a' && *p <= 'z') || (*p >= 'A' && *p <= 'Z') ||
+              (*p >= '0' && *p <= '9') || *p == '-' || *p == '_' || *p == '.')) return false;
+    /* Canonical zero padding prevents alternate encodings of the same job. */
+    for (const char *p = end; p < s + capacity; ++p) if (*p) return false;
+    return true;
+}
+static bool has_hash(const uint8_t hash[32])
+{
+    uint8_t any = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 32; ++i) any |= hash[i];
+    return any != 0;
+}
+static bool needs_backup(mosaico_character_phase_t phase)
+{
+    return phase != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED && phase != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CANCELED;
+}
+bool mosaico_character_image_header_valid(const uint8_t *head, size_t bytes, uint32_t image_bytes)
+{
+    static const uint8_t image_magic[8] = {'M','O','S','G','S','P',0,1};
+    if (!head || bytes != 64 || image_bytes < MIN_IMAGE_BYTES ||
+        memcmp(head, image_magic, 8) || head[8] != 1 || head[9] || head[10] != 64 || head[11] ||
+        get32(head + 12) != image_bytes - 64) return false;
+    for (unsigned i = 48; i < 64; ++i) if (head[i]) return false;
+    return true;
+}
+bool mosaico_character_record_is_initial(const mosaico_character_record_t *r)
+{
+    return mosaico_character_record_valid(r) &&
+        !strcmp(r->compat_version, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INITIAL_COMPAT) &&
+        !strcmp(r->character_version, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INITIAL_VERSION);
+}
+bool mosaico_character_record_valid(const mosaico_character_record_t *r)
+{
+    return r && r->sequence && r->phase >= MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED &&
+        r->phase <= MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_CONFIRMED && r->partition_address &&
+        r->partition_address % SECTOR_BYTES == 0 && r->partition_bytes &&
+        r->partition_bytes % SECTOR_BYTES == 0 &&
+        r->partition_address <= UINT32_MAX - r->partition_bytes &&
+        r->image_bytes >= MIN_IMAGE_BYTES && r->image_bytes <= r->partition_bytes &&
+        has_hash(r->image_sha256) && (!needs_backup(r->phase) || has_hash(r->backup_sha256)) &&
+        identifier(r->job, sizeof(r->job)) &&
+        identifier(r->compat_version, sizeof(r->compat_version)) &&
+        identifier(r->character_version, sizeof(r->character_version));
+}
+bool mosaico_character_record_encode(const mosaico_character_record_t *r,
+                                     uint8_t wire[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES])
+{
+    if (!wire || !mosaico_character_record_valid(r)) return false;
+    memset(wire, 0, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES);
+    memcpy(wire, magic, sizeof(magic));
+    put32(wire + 8, 1); put32(wire + 12, r->phase);
+    put32(wire + 16, (uint32_t)r->sequence); put32(wire + 20, (uint32_t)(r->sequence >> 32));
+    put32(wire + 24, r->partition_address); put32(wire + 28, r->partition_bytes);
+    put32(wire + 32, r->image_bytes);
+    memcpy(wire + 40, r->job, sizeof(r->job));
+    memcpy(wire + 104, r->image_sha256, 32); memcpy(wire + 136, r->backup_sha256, 32);
+    memcpy(wire + 168, r->compat_version, sizeof(r->compat_version));
+    memcpy(wire + 264, r->character_version, sizeof(r->character_version));
+    put32(wire + CRC_OFFSET, crc32(wire, CRC_OFFSET));
+    return true;
+}
+bool mosaico_character_record_decode(const uint8_t *wire, size_t bytes, mosaico_character_record_t *r)
+{
+    if (!wire || !r || bytes != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES ||
+        memcmp(wire, magic, sizeof(magic)) || get32(wire + 8) != 1 ||
+        get32(wire + CRC_OFFSET) != crc32(wire, CRC_OFFSET)) return false;
+    for (size_t i = 36; i < 40; ++i) if (wire[i]) return false;
+    for (size_t i = 328; i < CRC_OFFSET; ++i) if (wire[i]) return false;
+    memset(r, 0, sizeof(*r));
+    r->phase = (mosaico_character_phase_t)get32(wire + 12);
+    r->sequence = (uint64_t)get32(wire + 16) | (uint64_t)get32(wire + 20) << 32;
+    r->partition_address = get32(wire + 24); r->partition_bytes = get32(wire + 28);
+    r->image_bytes = get32(wire + 32);
+    memcpy(r->job, wire + 40, sizeof(r->job));
+    memcpy(r->image_sha256, wire + 104, 32); memcpy(r->backup_sha256, wire + 136, 32);
+    memcpy(r->compat_version, wire + 168, sizeof(r->compat_version));
+    memcpy(r->character_version, wire + 264, sizeof(r->character_version));
+    return mosaico_character_record_valid(r);
+}
+bool mosaico_character_transition_valid(const mosaico_character_record_t *a,
+                                        const mosaico_character_record_t *b)
+{
+    if (!mosaico_character_record_valid(a) || !mosaico_character_record_valid(b) ||
+        a->sequence == UINT64_MAX || b->sequence != a->sequence + 1 ||
+        a->partition_address != b->partition_address || a->partition_bytes != b->partition_bytes ||
+        a->image_bytes != b->image_bytes || memcmp(a->image_sha256, b->image_sha256, 32) ||
+        strcmp(a->job, b->job) || strcmp(a->compat_version, b->compat_version) ||
+        strcmp(a->character_version, b->character_version)) return false;
+    if (a->phase != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED && memcmp(a->backup_sha256, b->backup_sha256, 32)) return false;
+    switch (a->phase) {
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BACKUP_READY || b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CANCELED;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BACKUP_READY:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_WRITING || b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CANCELED;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_WRITING:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_TRIAL || b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_TRIAL:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CONFIRMED || b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK:
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_TRIAL;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_TRIAL:
+        /* Retrying a failed restored-app boot is an explicit USB maintenance
+         * action; coordinators must verify the full old NOR image first. */
+        return b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_CONFIRMED || b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK;
+    default:
+        return false;
+    }
+}
+mosaico_character_boot_action_t mosaico_character_boot_action(
+    const mosaico_character_record_t *r, bool frozen, const char *compat,
+    uint32_t address, uint32_t capacity)
+{
+    if (!mosaico_character_record_valid(r) || r->partition_address != address ||
+        r->partition_bytes != capacity) return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_HOLD;
+    switch (r->phase) {
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_WRITING:
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_TRIAL:
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING:
+        /* Restoration uses the old full image. A new firmware's compatibility
+         * identifier must never prevent recovery of an interrupted write. */
+        return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RESTORE;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK:
+        return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RETURN;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_TRIAL:
+        /* A failed restored-app boot must not automatically loop forever. */
+        return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_HOLD;
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED:
+    case MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BACKUP_READY:
+        return frozen && compat && !strcmp(r->compat_version, compat) ?
+            MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_INSTALL : MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_HOLD;
+    default:
+        return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_NORMAL;
+    }
+}
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal_store.c b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal_store.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fcf0593
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_journal_store.c
@@ -0,0 +1,253 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#include "mosaico_character_journal_store.h"
+#include "mosaico_nand_store.h"
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#ifdef _WIN32
+/* Host fault tests only; ESP-IDF uses POSIX VFS below. Windows rename does not
+ * replace an existing inactive slot, unlike the required LittleFS operation. */
+#include <io.h>
+#include <direct.h>
+#include <windows.h>
+#define journal_mkdir(path) _mkdir(path)
+#define journal_fsync(fd) _commit(fd)
+static int journal_rename(const char *from, const char *to)
+{
+    return MoveFileExA(from, to, MOVEFILE_REPLACE_EXISTING | MOVEFILE_WRITE_THROUGH) ? 0 : -1;
+}
+#else
+#define journal_mkdir(path) mkdir(path, 0700)
+#define journal_fsync(fd) fsync(fd)
+#define journal_rename(from, to) rename(from, to)
+#endif
+
+enum { PATH_BYTES = 256 };
+struct mosaico_character_journal_store_t {
+    char path[2][PATH_BYTES], temporary[PATH_BYTES];
+    mosaico_character_record_t records[2];
+    uint8_t wire[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES];
+    uint8_t verify[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES];
+    char directory[PATH_BYTES], selector[PATH_BYTES], scratch[PATH_BYTES];
+    mosaico_character_record_t seed;
+    bool selected;
+};
+static bool terminal(mosaico_character_phase_t phase)
+{
+    return phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CONFIRMED || phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_CONFIRMED ||
+        phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CANCELED;
+}
+static bool consecutive(const mosaico_character_record_t *a, const mosaico_character_record_t *b)
+{
+    if (mosaico_character_transition_valid(a, b)) return true;
+    /* Starting a later job is allowed only after the preceding transaction is
+     * terminal; retain a monotonically increasing sequence across all jobs. */
+    return terminal(a->phase) && b->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED &&
+        a->sequence != UINT64_MAX && b->sequence == a->sequence + 1 &&
+        strcmp(a->job, b->job) && a->partition_address == b->partition_address &&
+        a->partition_bytes == b->partition_bytes;
+}
+esp_err_t mosaico_character_journal_store_create(const char *directory,
+    mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t *out)
+{
+    if (!directory || !directory[0] || !out) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    *out = NULL;
+    mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h = calloc(1, sizeof(*h));
+    if (!h) return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM;
+    int a = snprintf(h->path[0], PATH_BYTES, "%s/transaction.0", directory);
+    int b = snprintf(h->path[1], PATH_BYTES, "%s/transaction.1", directory);
+    int c = snprintf(h->temporary, PATH_BYTES, "%s/transaction.partial", directory);
+    if (a < 0 || b < 0 || c < 0 || a >= PATH_BYTES || b >= PATH_BYTES || c >= PATH_BYTES) {
+        free(h); return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    }
+    strcpy(h->directory, directory);
+    c = snprintf(h->selector, PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-selector.record", directory);
+    if (c < 0 || c >= PATH_BYTES) { free(h); return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE; }
+    /* Creating a missing directory never initializes/formats its filesystem. */
+    if (journal_mkdir(directory) && errno != EEXIST) { free(h); return ESP_FAIL; }
+    struct stat st;
+    if (stat(directory, &st) || !S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)) { free(h); return ESP_FAIL; }
+    *out = h;
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+void mosaico_character_journal_store_delete(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h)
+{
+    free(h);
+}
+static esp_err_t read_slot(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h, unsigned slot)
+{
+    FILE *file = fopen(h->path[slot], "rb");
+    if (!file) return errno == ENOENT ? ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND : ESP_FAIL;
+    size_t bytes = fread(h->wire, 1, sizeof(h->wire), file);
+    int extra = fgetc(file);
+    bool ok = bytes == sizeof(h->wire) && extra == EOF && !ferror(file);
+    if (fclose(file)) ok = false;
+    return ok && mosaico_character_record_decode(h->wire, bytes, &h->records[slot]) ?
+        ESP_OK : ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+}
+static bool repair_seed_valid(const mosaico_character_record_t *r)
+{
+    return mosaico_character_record_valid(r) && r->sequence == 1 &&
+        r->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING && r->image_bytes == r->partition_bytes &&
+        !memcmp(r->image_sha256, r->backup_sha256, 32) &&
+        !strcmp(r->compat_version, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_REPAIR_COMPAT) &&
+        !strcmp(r->character_version, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_REPAIR_VERSION);
+}
+static esp_err_t select_history(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h)
+{
+    FILE *f = fopen(h->selector, "rb");
+    h->selected = false;
+    if (!f && errno != ENOENT) return ESP_FAIL;
+    if (f) {
+        bool ok = fread(h->wire, 1, sizeof(h->wire), f) == sizeof(h->wire) &&
+            fgetc(f) == EOF && !ferror(f);
+        if (fclose(f)) ok = false;
+        if (!ok || !mosaico_character_record_decode(h->wire, sizeof(h->wire), &h->seed) ||
+            !repair_seed_valid(&h->seed)) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+        h->selected = true;
+        int n = snprintf(h->scratch, PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-%s.seed", h->directory, h->seed.job);
+        if (n < 0 || n >= PATH_BYTES) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+        f = fopen(h->scratch, "rb");
+        if (!f) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+        ok = fread(h->verify, 1, sizeof(h->verify), f) == sizeof(h->verify) &&
+            fgetc(f) == EOF && !ferror(f) && !memcmp(h->wire, h->verify, sizeof(h->wire));
+        if (fclose(f)) ok = false;
+        if (!ok) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {
+        int n = h->selected ? snprintf(h->path[i], PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-%s.%u", h->directory, h->seed.job, i) :
+            snprintf(h->path[i], PATH_BYTES, "%s/transaction.%u", h->directory, i);
+        if (n < 0 || n >= PATH_BYTES) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    }
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+static esp_err_t load_latest(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h, unsigned *latest)
+{
+    esp_err_t selected = select_history(h);
+    if (selected != ESP_OK) return selected;
+    esp_err_t a = read_slot(h, 0), b = read_slot(h, 1);
+    if ((a != ESP_OK && a != ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND) || (b != ESP_OK && b != ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND))
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    if (a == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND && b == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND) {
+        if (!h->selected) return ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND;
+        /* A durable selector is itself the initial recovery intent. A reboot
+         * before the first transition must restore, never treat this as empty. */
+        h->records[0] = h->seed; *latest = 0; return ESP_OK;
+    }
+    if (a == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND || b == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND) {
+        *latest = a == ESP_OK ? 0 : 1;
+        /* The first save must be STAGED, sequence 1. A lone later slot means
+         * committed history disappeared; never infer it is safe to boot. */
+        if (h->selected) return consecutive(&h->seed, &h->records[*latest]) ? ESP_OK : ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+        return h->records[*latest].sequence == 1 &&
+            h->records[*latest].phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED ? ESP_OK : ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    *latest = h->records[0].sequence > h->records[1].sequence ? 0 : 1;
+    return consecutive(&h->records[1 - *latest], &h->records[*latest]) ?
+        ESP_OK : ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+}
+esp_err_t mosaico_character_journal_store_load(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h,
+    mosaico_character_record_t *out)
+{
+    if (!h || !out) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    unsigned latest = 0;
+    esp_err_t err = load_latest(h, &latest);
+    if (err == ESP_OK) *out = h->records[latest];
+    return err;
+}
+static esp_err_t publish_record(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h,
+    const char *path, const mosaico_character_record_t *record)
+{
+    if (!mosaico_character_record_encode(record, h->wire)) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    FILE *file = fopen(h->temporary, "wb");
+    if (!file) return ESP_FAIL;
+    bool ok = fwrite(h->wire, 1, sizeof(h->wire), file) == sizeof(h->wire);
+    if (ok && fflush(file)) ok = false;
+    if (ok && journal_fsync(fileno(file))) ok = false;
+    if (fclose(file)) ok = false;
+    if (!ok) return ESP_FAIL;
+    file = fopen(h->temporary, "rb");
+    if (!file) return ESP_FAIL;
+    ok = fread(h->verify, 1, sizeof(h->verify), file) == sizeof(h->verify);
+    int extra = fgetc(file);
+    ok = ok && extra == EOF && !ferror(file) && !memcmp(h->verify, h->wire, sizeof(h->wire));
+    if (fclose(file)) ok = false;
+    if (!ok) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    esp_err_t err = mosaico_nand_store_sync();
+    if (err != ESP_OK) return err;
+    if (journal_rename(h->temporary, path)) return ESP_FAIL;
+    return mosaico_nand_store_sync();
+}
+
+esp_err_t mosaico_character_journal_store_save(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h,
+    const mosaico_character_record_t *record)
+{
+    if (!h || !mosaico_character_record_valid(record)) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    unsigned latest = 0, target = 0;
+    esp_err_t err = load_latest(h, &latest);
+    if (err == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND) {
+        if (record->sequence != 1 || record->phase != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    } else if (err == ESP_OK) {
+        if (!consecutive(&h->records[latest], record)) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+        target = 1 - latest;
+    } else return err;
+    return publish_record(h, h->path[target], record);
+}
+
+static esp_err_t preserve_selector(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h)
+{
+    FILE *in = fopen(h->selector, "rb");
+    if (!in) return errno == ENOENT ? ESP_OK : ESP_FAIL;
+    FILE *out = fopen(h->temporary, "wb");
+    if (!out) { fclose(in); return ESP_FAIL; }
+    bool ok = true; size_t n;
+    while ((n = fread(h->wire, 1, sizeof(h->wire), in)) != 0)
+        if (fwrite(h->wire, 1, n, out) != n) { ok = false; break; }
+    if (ferror(in) || fflush(out) || journal_fsync(fileno(out))) ok = false;
+    if (fclose(in)) ok = false;
+    if (fclose(out)) ok = false;
+    if (!ok) return ESP_FAIL;
+    in = fopen(h->selector, "rb"); out = fopen(h->temporary, "rb");
+    if (!in || !out) { if(in)fclose(in);if(out)fclose(out);return ESP_FAIL; }
+    do {
+        n = fread(h->wire, 1, sizeof(h->wire), in);
+        if (fread(h->verify, 1, sizeof(h->verify), out) != n || memcmp(h->wire, h->verify, n)) ok = false;
+    } while (ok && n == sizeof(h->wire));
+    if (ferror(in) || ferror(out)) ok = false;
+    if (fclose(in)) ok = false;
+    if (fclose(out)) ok = false;
+    if (!ok) return ESP_FAIL;
+    esp_err_t err = mosaico_nand_store_sync();
+    if (err == ESP_OK && journal_rename(h->temporary, h->scratch)) err = ESP_FAIL;
+    if (err == ESP_OK) err = mosaico_nand_store_sync();
+    return err;
+}
+
+esp_err_t mosaico_character_journal_store_repair(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t h,
+    const mosaico_character_record_t *seed)
+{
+    if (!h || !repair_seed_valid(seed)) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    unsigned latest;
+    esp_err_t current = load_latest(h, &latest);
+    if (current != ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE) return current == ESP_OK ? ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE : current;
+    /* Require a unique repair ID; never replace a prior recovery history. */
+    const char *suffix[] = {"seed", "prior", "0", "1"};
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+        int n = snprintf(h->scratch, PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-%s.%s", h->directory, seed->job, suffix[i]);
+        if (n < 0 || n >= PATH_BYTES) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+        struct stat st;
+        if (!stat(h->scratch, &st) || errno != ENOENT) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    int n = snprintf(h->scratch, PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-%s.prior", h->directory, seed->job);
+    if (n < 0 || n >= PATH_BYTES) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    esp_err_t err = preserve_selector(h);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) return err;
+    n = snprintf(h->scratch, PATH_BYTES, "%s/repair-%s.seed", h->directory, seed->job);
+    if (n < 0 || n >= PATH_BYTES) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    err = publish_record(h, h->scratch, seed);
+    if (err == ESP_OK) err = publish_record(h, h->selector, seed);
+    return err;
+}
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_transaction.c b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_transaction.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1965167
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/character_transaction.c
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#include "mosaico_character_transaction.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+static esp_err_t advance(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t store,
+    mosaico_character_record_t *r, mosaico_character_phase_t phase)
+{
+    if (r->sequence == UINT64_MAX) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    ++r->sequence; r->phase = phase;
+    /* Caller must exit on save failure. Never write NOR using an uncertain
+     * in-memory phase; a later boot reloads the actual committed record. */
+    return mosaico_character_journal_store_save(store, r);
+}
+static esp_err_t restore(mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t store,
+    const mosaico_character_transaction_ops_t *ops, mosaico_character_record_t *r,
+    mosaico_character_transaction_result_t *result)
+{
+    esp_err_t err = ops->verify_backup(ops->context, r);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) return err;
+    if (r->phase != MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING) {
+        err = advance(store, r, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING);
+        if (err != ESP_OK) return err;
+    }
+    err = ops->restore_backup(ops->context, r);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) return err;
+    err = advance(store, r, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK);
+    if (err == ESP_OK) *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_NORMAL;
+    return err;
+}
+esp_err_t mosaico_character_transaction_run(
+    mosaico_character_journal_store_handle_t store,
+    const mosaico_character_transaction_ops_t *ops, bool frozen, const char *compat,
+    uint32_t address, uint32_t capacity, mosaico_character_transaction_result_t *result)
+{
+    if (!store || !ops || !result || !ops->verify_candidate || !ops->backup ||
+        !ops->verify_backup || !ops->write_candidate || !ops->restore_backup) return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_HOLD;
+    mosaico_character_record_t *r = calloc(1, sizeof(*r));
+    if (!r) return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM;
+    esp_err_t err = mosaico_character_journal_store_load(store, r);
+    if (err == ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND) {
+        *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_NORMAL; err = ESP_OK; goto done;
+    }
+    if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+    mosaico_character_boot_action_t action = mosaico_character_boot_action(r, frozen, compat, address, capacity);
+    if (action == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_HOLD) { err = ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE; goto done; }
+    if (action == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_NORMAL) {
+        *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_NORMAL; goto done;
+    }
+    /* ROLLED_BACK is a durable return handoff. No repeated NOR erase; the
+     * Recovery coordinator verifies active old resources and boots the app. */
+    if (action == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RETURN) {
+        *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_NORMAL; goto done;
+    }
+    if (action == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RESTORE) {
+        err = restore(store, ops, r, result); goto done;
+    }
+    err = ops->verify_candidate(ops->context, r);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+    if (r->phase == MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED) {
+        err = ops->backup(ops->context, r->backup_sha256);
+        if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+        err = advance(store, r, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BACKUP_READY);
+        if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+    }
+    err = ops->verify_backup(ops->context, r);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+    err = advance(store, r, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_WRITING);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) goto done;
+    err = ops->write_candidate(ops->context, r);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) {
+        err = restore(store, ops, r, result); goto done;
+    }
+    err = advance(store, r, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_TRIAL);
+    if (err == ESP_OK) *result = MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESULT_TRIAL;
+done:
+    free(r);
+    return err;
+}
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_install_policy.h b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_install_policy.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..af4ca91
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_install_policy.h
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#pragma once
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+/* Build-owned admission shared by staging, trial and Recovery. Empty/default
+ * policy admits no downloaded image. An optional exact job limits validation
+ * builds; remote commands cannot change either build-owned setting. */
+static inline const char *mosaico_character_install_compat(void)
+{
+#ifdef MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INSTALL_COMPAT
+    return MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INSTALL_COMPAT;
+#else
+    return NULL;
+#endif
+}
+static inline bool mosaico_character_install_admitted(const char *job, const char *compat)
+{
+    const char *expected = mosaico_character_install_compat();
+    if (!job || !compat || !expected || strcmp(compat, expected)) return false;
+#ifdef MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INSTALL_JOB
+    if (strcmp(job, MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INSTALL_JOB)) return false;
+#endif
+    return true;
+}
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_journal.h b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_journal.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5513054
--- /dev/null
+++ b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_journal.h
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#pragma once
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+/* Product-owned resource transaction ABI. Explicit wire encoding, no native
+ * structs on disk. This module never writes NOR or authorizes a candidate pack.
+ * One update coordinator owns all load/transition/save calls; no shared tasks. */
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES 512U
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_JOB_BYTES 64U
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_COMPAT_BYTES 96U
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_VERSION_BYTES 64U
+/* Reserved LOCAL source tags, never accepted by the external pack validator.
+ * Initial restore still requires the product's trusted installation gate. */
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INITIAL_COMPAT "muse-protected-initial-v1"
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_INITIAL_VERSION "protected-initial"
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_REPAIR_COMPAT "muse-journal-repair-v1"
+#define MOSAICO_CHARACTER_REPAIR_VERSION "protected-initial-repair"
+
+typedef enum {
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_STAGED = 1,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BACKUP_READY,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_WRITING,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_TRIAL,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CONFIRMED,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RESTORING,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLED_BACK,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_CANCELED,
+    /* ROLLED_BACK means NOR restored, not yet accepted by the application.
+     * These appended states preserve existing wire values. */
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_TRIAL,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_ROLLBACK_CONFIRMED,
+} mosaico_character_phase_t;
+
+typedef struct {
+    uint64_t sequence;
+    mosaico_character_phase_t phase;
+    uint32_t partition_address, partition_bytes, image_bytes;
+    uint8_t image_sha256[32], backup_sha256[32];
+    char job[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_JOB_BYTES];
+    char compat_version[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_COMPAT_BYTES];
+    char character_version[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_VERSION_BYTES];
+} mosaico_character_record_t;
+
+typedef enum {
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_NORMAL,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_INSTALL,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RESTORE,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_HOLD,
+    MOSAICO_CHARACTER_BOOT_RETURN,
+} mosaico_character_boot_action_t;
+
+bool mosaico_character_record_valid(const mosaico_character_record_t *record);
+bool mosaico_character_record_is_initial(const mosaico_character_record_t *record);
+/* Product MOSGSP outer header: little-endian uint16 version=1 and
+ * uint16 header_size=64, uint32 payload length, SHA-256, zero reserved bytes. */
+bool mosaico_character_image_header_valid(const uint8_t *header, size_t header_bytes,
+    uint32_t image_bytes);
+bool mosaico_character_record_encode(const mosaico_character_record_t *record,
+                                     uint8_t wire[MOSAICO_CHARACTER_RECORD_BYTES]);
+bool mosaico_character_record_decode(const uint8_t *wire, size_t bytes,
+                                     mosaico_character_record_t *record);
+/* destination is prepared by caller (e.g. backup hash added). Immutable task
+ * fields and backup hashes after BACKUP_READY may never change. Save only after
+ * the corresponding side effect is durable and read-back verified. */
+bool mosaico_character_transition_valid(const mosaico_character_record_t *from,
+                                        const mosaico_character_record_t *to);
+/* frozen_compat is trusted firmware policy; false MUST reject even a matching
+ * candidate identifier. Address/capacity must come from the live partition. */
+mosaico_character_boot_action_t mosaico_character_boot_action(
+    const mosaico_character_record_t *record, bool frozen_compat,
+    const char *compat_version, uint32_t address, uint32_t capacity);
diff --git a/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_journal_store.h b/esp-mosaico-vibe-mode/components/esp_mosaico_character_journal/include/mosaico_character_journal_store.h
